      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Map the thread to an output spot (row, col) with the global index formula.\n\n2. Check the bounds. We round up, so some threads fall outside; they stay here.\n\n3. Linearize: work out where the spot is in memory and where the inputs it needs are.\n\n4. Read those inputs and calculate the result.\n\n5. Write the result to the output spot.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Map the thread to an output spot (row, col) with the global index formula.\n\n2. Check the bounds. We round up, so some threads fall outside; they stay here.\n\n3. Linearize: work out where the spot is in memory and where the inputs it needs are.\n\n4. Read those inputs and calculate the result.\n\n5. Write the result to the output spot.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
